cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MeijerG.jl in your research, please cite the archived software using the metadata below."
title: "MeijerG.jl: Numerical evaluation of the Meijer G-function in Julia"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gutleb
    given-names: Timon S.
    affiliation: University of Leeds
    email: T.S.Gutleb@leeds.ac.uk
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19430427
repository-code: "https://github.com/TSGut/MeijerG.jl"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19430427"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Julia
  - Meijer G-function
  - special functions
  - numerical analysis
  - Mellin-Barnes integrals
abstract: >-
  MeijerG.jl is a Julia package for numerical evaluation of the Meijer
  G-function using a guarded polyalgorithm of special-function reductions,
  Slater residue expansions, confluence-aware evaluation, and numerical
  Mellin-Barnes contour integration.
